content.p:
Secondly, regulation 97V(4) requires appellants to state the grounds of appeal.  Unlike similar provisions elsewhere in the PAYE Regulations, there is no attempt in the regulations to curtail the grounds of appeal (cf regulations 72A(4), (5), 72B, 72C, 72G, 81A, 97LF, 97U, 99 and 210C

 This list omits those provisions added subsequent to the introduction of regulation 97V.
		  ).  We note that regulation 97U is in fact part of the code at which we are looking.
